---
// Written from what the app does today (see travel-app/README.md and
// docs/plan.md). Live and in Google, but still to be reviewed before launch.
// When the app sends email, add the email service under "How we share
// information". Change "Last updated" whenever this changes.
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../site.config";

const metaDescription =
  "What Travel Map & Journal keeps about you, who can see it, the services it uses for maps, search and exchange rates, and how to download or delete it.";
---

<LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy" description={metaDescription} updated="November 11, 2026">
  <div>
    <p>
      {site.legalName} ("we", "us" or "our") runs {site.name}, a private travel journal (the "App"), and this website (the "Site"). This
      policy explains what we keep, who can see it, and what you can do about it.
    </p>
    <p>The short version: what you add is yours and private unless you share it, nothing is sold, and there are no ads.</p>
  </div>

  <section>
    <h2>Information we collect</h2>

    <div>
      <h3>1) Your account</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Your name and email address</li>
        <li>Your password, stored only as a one-way hash we can't read</li>
        <li>If you sign in with Google: your name, email and profile photo from Google</li>
        <li>Your settings: your home currency, your home (a city, state or country) and light or dark</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h3>2) What you add</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Trips, spots, notes, ratings, homes and past homes, and your wishlist</li>
        <li>Expenses, who went on a trip (names you type, which needn't be real names) and how costs were split</li>
        <li>One cover photo per trip or home, if you add one</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="note">
        <p>
          <strong>Photos:</strong> location data and other details your camera saves inside a photo are removed when it's uploaded. Photos
          are stored privately and shown only to the people who can see that trip.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h3>3) Logins and security</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Each device you're logged in on, with its IP address and browser, so you can log the others out in Settings</li>
        <li>Counts of attempts (such as wrong passwords and searches) to stop abuse, kept for a short time</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h3>4) Usage counts</h3>
      <p>
        That an account opened the App on a given day, and daily totals (such as how many searches were made). These are counts only: we
        never look at what anyone wrote or where they went to make them.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h3>5) Messages you send us</h3>
      <p>
        When you use the contact form on the Site, we collect your name, your email address and what you write, so we can answer you.
      </p>
      <div class="note">
        <p>
          <strong>Note:</strong> the contact form is processed by Basin, which receives and stores your message on our behalf. Basin's own
          practices are in its privacy policy at
          <a href="https://usebasin.com/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">usebasin.com/privacy</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h3>6) Analytics</h3>
      <p>
        We use Cloudflare Web Analytics on the Site and the App to see which pages are visited. It uses no cookies, doesn't follow you
        between websites, and gives us totals such as page views, referring pages, country, and browser and device type.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How we use information</h2>
    <p>We use it to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Run the App for you: show your trips, maps, totals and share links</li>
      <li>Keep accounts secure and stop spam and abuse</li>
      <li>Answer you when you write to us</li>
      <li>Understand, in totals, how the App is used, so we can improve it</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We don't use what you add for advertising, and we don't sell or rent it to anyone.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Who can see what you add</h2>
    <p>Only you, unless you share. There's no public profile, feed or followers.</p>
    <div class="items">
      <div>
        <h4>Share links</h4>
        <p>
          A share link shows a read-only page of one trip or place to anyone who has the link. A spots-only link never shows costs or who
          went. Stopping sharing deletes the link. Your wishlist, and where and when you've lived, are never on a share link.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4>People on a trip</h4>
        <p>People who join a trip you've shared with them see that trip, including its expenses, and can add to it if you allow it.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4>The demo</h4>
        <p>The demo account on the Site is filled with made-up trips. Nothing anyone types in the demo is saved.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>The App sets only the cookies it needs to work:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>One that keeps you logged in</li>
      <li>Small ones that remember light or dark, how you last logged in, and that you've opened the App today</li>
    </ul>
    <p>None of them are for advertising or follow you to other websites. The Site itself sets no cookies.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How we share information</h2>
    <p>We don't sell your personal information. We share it only in these cases:</p>
    <div class="items">
      <div>
        <h4>Service providers</h4>
        <p>Services that help run the App, and only what each needs:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts the Site, the App, its database and photos, checks that sign-ups and contact form messages come from a person (Turnstile), and provides the analytics above.</li>
          <li><strong>Photon</strong> (OpenStreetMap) answers place searches. What you type in a search is sent; your account isn't.</li>
          <li><strong>OpenFreeMap</strong> serves the map tiles your browser shows.</li>
          <li><strong>Frankfurter</strong> supplies European Central Bank exchange rates. No personal information is sent.</li>
          <li><strong>Google</strong>, only if you choose to sign in with Google.</li>
          <li><strong>Basin</strong> receives what you send through the Site's contact form.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4>Legal and safety</h4>
        <p>If the law requires it, or to protect the rights, safety or property of our users, the public or us.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4>Business transfers</h4>
        <p>
          If the App is ever sold or merged, your information may pass to the new owner, who must keep to this policy or tell you before
          changing it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      What you add is kept until you delete it or your account. Deleting your account deletes your trips, spots, expenses, photos, wishlist
      and share links; spots you added to someone else's trip pass to that trip's owner. Deleted information may remain in the database's
      backups for up to 30 days before it's gone for good. Usage counts are kept as totals.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      Everything is sent over an encrypted connection, passwords are stored as hashes, photos are private, and every page checks that you're
      allowed to see it. No method of storage or transmission is completely secure, so we can't promise absolute security.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Download your data:</strong> in Settings, everything you've written in one file, any time</li>
      <li><strong>Change or delete</strong> anything you've added, whenever you like</li>
      <li><strong>Stop sharing:</strong> deleting a share link stops it working at once</li>
      <li><strong>Delete your account</strong> in Settings</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have other rights, such as asking what we hold about you or asking us to correct it. Write to us
      and we'll help.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The App isn't meant for children under 13, and we don't knowingly collect personal information from them. If you think a child has
      made an account, write to us and we'll delete it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>
      Spots have links to Google Maps, and the App links to other websites. Once you follow one, that site's own privacy policy applies, not
      this one.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy. We'll post the new version here and change the date at the top, and if a change matters for what we do
      with your information, we'll tell you by email before it takes effect.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
